WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.919
- Write a composition on the subtle

00:00:01.919 --> 00:00:03.900
philosophy of the round and-

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.358
No.

00:00:05.358 --> 00:00:08.858
(mellow percussion music)

00:00:09.817 --> 00:00:11.515
- [Narrator] The gaokao is China's intense

00:00:11.515 --> 00:00:13.442
two-day college entrance exam.

00:00:13.442 --> 00:00:16.335
Students' marks on the
exam are said to determine

00:00:16.335 --> 00:00:18.668
their entire future life opportunities

00:00:18.668 --> 00:00:20.751
and earning potential in China.

00:00:20.751 --> 00:00:23.055
With the belief that those
who Excel on the test

00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:26.273
will have the best careers
and even marriage prospects.

00:00:26.273 --> 00:00:29.108
College entrance is especially
competitive in China,

00:00:29.108 --> 00:00:31.224
where the top universities only select

00:00:31.224 --> 00:00:34.122
as few as 1 in 50,000 students.

00:00:34.122 --> 00:00:35.584
- Wow!

00:00:35.584 --> 00:00:36.779
That's pretty low.

00:00:36.779 --> 00:00:39.118
That's like 0.002%?

00:00:39.118 --> 00:00:40.263
- [Narrator] The test is so important

00:00:40.263 --> 00:00:41.596
that factories and buildings

00:00:41.596 --> 00:00:44.032
will shut down while the exam is underway

00:00:44.032 --> 00:00:47.125
as police cars patrol
to keep streets quiet.

00:00:47.125 --> 00:00:50.223
Ambulances are placed
outside exam facilities

00:00:50.223 --> 00:00:52.725
in case of nervous collapses.

00:00:52.725 --> 00:00:56.337
The multiple choice questions
are notoriously hard

00:00:56.337 --> 00:00:57.835
with questions such as...

00:00:57.835 --> 00:00:58.668
- Last October,

00:00:58.668 --> 00:01:00.755
President Xi Jinping said that

00:01:00.755 --> 00:01:02.665
while art is based on imagination,

00:01:02.665 --> 00:01:05.319
- It should still be down-to-earth.

00:01:05.319 --> 00:01:07.586
- There may be hundreds
of ways to create art,

00:01:07.586 --> 00:01:08.593
the best way, however,

00:01:08.593 --> 00:01:11.222
is to trace back to the
people's daily lives

00:01:11.222 --> 00:01:12.940
and create something based off that.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:16.112
- From a materialism point
of view, this is because

00:01:16.112 --> 00:01:19.649
One, art originates from
the daily lives of people.

00:01:19.649 --> 00:01:22.081
Two, art depends on innovation.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:24.591
Three, the way art reflects on society

00:01:24.591 --> 00:01:27.415
and its style is unified.

00:01:27.415 --> 00:01:31.508
Four, art is a form of ideology
that reflects people's lives

00:01:31.508 --> 00:01:35.252
while at the same time serving the people.

00:01:35.252 --> 00:01:36.891
- God, this is confusing.

00:01:36.891 --> 00:01:37.724
- I don't-

00:01:37.724 --> 00:01:38.999
I have no idea.

00:01:38.999 --> 00:01:41.677
- It's like kind of a logic question,

00:01:41.677 --> 00:01:44.062
but it's also a grammar question

00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:48.329
and it's also related to
current events and politics?

00:01:48.329 --> 00:01:49.863
- Just reading this gives me anxiety

00:01:49.863 --> 00:01:52.791
so I can understand why people
have ambulances outside.

00:01:52.791 --> 00:01:53.624
- I don't know.

00:01:53.624 --> 00:01:54.457
I'm gonna say A.

00:01:54.457 --> 00:01:55.317
- I'm gonna go B,

00:01:55.317 --> 00:01:56.979
one and four.

00:01:56.979 --> 00:01:57.812
- D.

00:01:57.812 --> 00:01:58.645
- [Man] You're correct!

00:01:58.645 --> 00:01:59.699
(bell ding)

00:01:59.699 --> 00:02:00.532
- Heck yeah!

00:02:00.532 --> 00:02:02.918
- But literally, it's
saying the same thing.

00:02:02.918 --> 00:02:05.105
- [Narrator] The gaokao
has been seen as symbolic

00:02:05.105 --> 00:02:07.986
of the Chinese education
system as a whole,

00:02:07.986 --> 00:02:10.369
and both the exam and the system itself

00:02:10.369 --> 00:02:12.357
have been criticized for putting

00:02:12.357 --> 00:02:14.488
impossible pressures on teens.

00:02:14.488 --> 00:02:18.478
Outbreaks of suicides
accompany every exam season.

00:02:18.478 --> 00:02:19.561
- Wow.

00:02:19.561 --> 00:02:22.246
- If your whole life depends on this exam,

00:02:22.246 --> 00:02:24.921
that's so much pressure
for one person to handle,

00:02:24.921 --> 00:02:27.107
especially if you're
still growing as an adult.

00:02:27.107 --> 00:02:30.522
- I mean if this one test determines

00:02:30.522 --> 00:02:32.108
what happens in your life,

00:02:32.108 --> 00:02:34.052
that is really intense.

00:02:34.052 --> 00:02:36.592
- [Narrator] The exam also
includes a number of essays

00:02:36.592 --> 00:02:39.648
with prompts than can
be notoriously obtuse,

00:02:39.648 --> 00:02:40.861
such as...

00:02:40.861 --> 00:02:43.694
- Do butterfly wings have colors?

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:50.198
- Hold up.

00:02:50.198 --> 00:02:52.636
- Why is this an essay question?

00:02:52.636 --> 00:02:54.122
Who do you admire the most?

00:02:54.122 --> 00:02:56.317
A biotechnology researcher,

00:02:56.317 --> 00:02:58.254
- A welding engineer technician,

00:02:58.254 --> 00:02:59.951
- Or a photographer.?

00:02:59.951 --> 00:03:01.940
What the heck?

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:04.900
That's just a personality question.

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:06.896
- I'm so stressed.

00:03:06.896 --> 00:03:08.973
- [Narrator] Cheating has
been a rampant problem,

00:03:08.973 --> 00:03:11.026
including the use of spy cameras

00:03:11.026 --> 00:03:15.082
and radio devices to transmit
questions and answers.

00:03:15.082 --> 00:03:16.876
Those who are caught cheating

00:03:16.876 --> 00:03:19.168
may spend up to seven years in prison.

00:03:19.168 --> 00:03:21.534
To try to prevent students
from pursuing their

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.903
increasingly creative methods of cheating,

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:26.494
drones have been used as hall monitors.

00:03:26.494 --> 00:03:27.730
- Whoa!

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:28.994
- Drones!

00:03:28.994 --> 00:03:29.971
- People are cheating so much

00:03:29.971 --> 00:03:32.192
that they have drones in charge?

00:03:32.192 --> 00:03:33.857
- This reminds me of Minority Report,

00:03:33.857 --> 00:03:36.223
like robots are surveillance.

00:03:36.223 --> 00:03:38.874
- The containers for milk
are always square boxes.

00:03:38.874 --> 00:03:41.783
Containers for mineral water
are always round bottles.

00:03:41.783 --> 00:03:46.502
- Round wine bottles are
usually placed in square boxes.

00:03:46.502 --> 00:03:48.570
- Write a composition
on the subtle philosophy

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:50.509
of the round and square.

00:03:50.509 --> 00:03:51.342
Oh my God,

00:03:52.188 --> 00:03:53.021
what?

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.584
These are so broad!

00:03:55.584 --> 00:03:58.341
What do you even say here?

00:03:58.341 --> 00:04:00.439
- I think just humanity has gotten

00:04:00.439 --> 00:04:02.828
way too obsessed with tests.

00:04:02.828 --> 00:04:05.401
There are other ways to evaluate people.

00:04:05.401 --> 00:04:08.588
- Compared to what we
have here in America,

00:04:08.588 --> 00:04:10.556
we're pretty, pretty lucky.

00:04:10.556 --> 00:04:12.239
- It just seems like if

00:04:12.239 --> 00:04:16.081
you're putting so much
pressure on a young kid,

00:04:16.081 --> 00:04:18.394
about a standardized test,

00:04:18.394 --> 00:04:19.892
something's not right.

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:24.807
- I hope they relax their
systems at some point because

00:04:24.807 --> 00:04:27.963
I can't imagine even going through that.

00:04:27.963 --> 00:04:29.419
- [Male Interviewee] I'm
just thinking more about

00:04:29.419 --> 00:04:32.669
what is the sole philosophy
of the round and square?

00:04:32.669 --> 00:04:35.106
(lighthearted music)

